    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nFor Sale by DNG Online Auction TO REGISTER FOR OUR ONLINE AUCTION on the 30th September 2026 at 3pm.Visit www.dngauctions.ieChoose/ Search for your property of interest, click log in & register to bid and follow the necessary steps.Bidder security required prior to auction date in order to successfully bid on the day.\n\nDNG Martin O'Connor Estate Agents are delighted to present to the market this attractive roadside parcel of land extending to approximately 0.37 Ha (0.91 Acres), superbly positioned on the N59 Galway to Clifden Road, just minutes from the bustling village of Oughterard.\n\nThis easily accessible parcel enjoys excellent road frontage and offers a wonderful opportunity to acquire a manageable holding in one of Connemara's most desirable locations. Whether you're seeking a hobby farm, additional grazing land, a paddock for animals, recreational ground, or simply a long-term land investment, this property offers endless possibilities (subject to any necessary statutory consents).\n\nThe land is conveniently located just outside Oughterard Village, where an excellent range of shops, cafés, schools, restaurants and sporting amenities are available. Lough Corrib, renowned for its world-class trout and salmon fishing, is only moments away, while the surrounding Connemara countryside offers endless opportunities for walking, cycling and outdoor pursuits. Galway City is approximately 25 km from the property, making it an ideal rural retreat with excellent accessibility.\n\nParcels of land of this size and in such a convenient location rarely come to the market. The property's prominent roadside position, ease of access and proximity to Oughterard make it an appealing purchase for local landowners, hobby farmers, equestrian enthusiasts, gardeners, or those looking to secure a landholding for future generations.\n\nPlease note this property will be offered by online auction (unless sold prior). Vendors may decide to accept pre-auction bids so please register your interest with us to avoid disappointment. The successful bidder is required to pay the balance of 10% deposit and contracts are signed immediately on acceptance of a bid.\n\nViewing is highly recommended.\n\nDirections\n\nFrom Oughterard Village, travel west on the N59 towards Clifden. The property is located approximately 2 km from the village centre on the left-hand side and is identified by a DNG Martin O'Connor For Sale sign."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Extending to approximately 0.37 Ha (0.91 Acres)</li><li> Excellent frontage onto the N59 GalwayClifden Road</li><li> Just minutes from Oughterard Village</li><li> Approx. 25 km from Galway City</li><li> Easily accessible roadside holding</li><li> Ideal hobby farm, paddock or recreational land</li><li> Suitable for grazing, gardening or amenity use</li><li> Attractive long-term land investment</li><li> Close to Lough Corrib and the gateway to Connemara</li><li> For Sale by DNG Online Auction (unless previously sold)</ul>"
      },
